From: muOS Developer
Date: Sat, 9 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Force application-side display rotation via PPSSPP_DISPLAY_ROTATION

Some Mali Vulkan drivers using VK_KHR_display (e.g. Rockchip rk3576)
report only VK_SURFACE_TRANSFORM_IDENTITY_BIT_KHR in surfCapabilities_,
even when the panel is physically mounted rotated 90/180/270 degrees and
the application must compensate.  These drivers also fix the surface
extent at the panel-natural resolution (min == max == currentExtent),
making the standard ARM "surface rotation" pattern (where preTransform
and a swapped swapchain extent let the driver handle rotation) unusable.

This patch lets the user force application-side rotation via the
environment variable PPSSPP_DISPLAY_ROTATION (values: 0, 90, 180, 270).
When set, PPSSPP's existing rotation infrastructure (g_display.rotation,
RotateRectToDisplay, the rotated curWidth/curHeight handling in
VulkanRenderManager) is engaged regardless of what the driver advertises.

To support drivers that won't accept rotated swapchain extents, the
"backbuffer dimensions" exposed to the UI layer are split from the actual
"swapchain image dimensions" used for VkImage resource sizing:

  GetBackbufferWidth/Height       -> swapChainExtent_     (logical/post-rotation)
  GetSwapchainImageWidth/Height   -> swapchainImageExtent_ (physical/native)

In the normal case (no rotation, or driver-side rotation on Android) both
extents are kept in sync and the new getters return identical values; the
existing rotation block now swaps both extents together, so the existing
Android path is preserved.  Under PPSSPP_DISPLAY_ROTATION only
swapChainExtent_ is swapped, so the UI lays out for the logical landscape
size while VkImage objects (swapchain images, depth buffer, framebuffer,
backbuffer renderpass area, RotateRectToDisplay destination dims) all
continue to use the physical panel-native size that the driver enforces.

VulkanRenderManager's curWidth_/curHeight_ derivation has to handle both
arrangements: when driver-side rotation is in effect, swapchain image dims
match the post-rotation logical dims and the existing swap is correct;
when application-side rotation is in effect, swapchain images stay at
physical dims while GetBackbufferWidth/Height already report logical dims
(already "swapped"), so the swap must NOT be repeated.  The patch detects
this by comparing GetBackbufferWidth/Height vs GetSwapchainImageWidth/
Height -- if they differ, application-side rotation is active and the
swap is skipped, so renderArea ends up at the correct logical dims that
RotateRectToDisplay then maps onto the physical swapchain image.

Usage example for rk3576 with fbcon=rotate:3 and a panel mounted rotated
90 degrees:

  export SDL_KMSDRM_ORIENTATION=0      # SDL hands PPSSPP a portrait window
  export PPSSPP_DISPLAY_ROTATION=270   # PPSSPP rotates render output 270 CW
  /path/to/PPSSPP

The matching SDL2 patch in the muOS tree skips RGA rotation for Vulkan
windows; this PPSSPP patch is what produces a correctly-oriented landscape
display (UI + game) on a rotated portrait panel.

Files modified:
  Common/GPU/Vulkan/VulkanContext.h           (new field, new getters)
  Common/GPU/Vulkan/VulkanContext.cpp         (env var override, sync logic)
  Common/GPU/Vulkan/VulkanQueueRunner.cpp     (use physical dims internally)
  Common/GPU/Vulkan/VulkanRenderManager.cpp   (curWidth/curHeight handling,
                                               framebuffer creation)
---
diff -urpN a/Common/GPU/Vulkan/VulkanContext.cpp b/Common/GPU/Vulkan/VulkanContext.cpp
--- a/Common/GPU/Vulkan/VulkanContext.cpp	2026-05-09 23:34:27.445146341 +0000
+++ b/Common/GPU/Vulkan/VulkanContext.cpp	2026-05-09 23:35:49.879130915 +0000
@@ -1391,6 +1391,7 @@ bool VulkanContext::InitSwapchain(VkPres
 	if (surfCapabilities_.maxImageExtent.width == 0 || surfCapabilities_.maxImageExtent.height == 0) {
 		WARN_LOG(Log::G3D, "Max image extent is 0 - app is probably minimized. Faking having a swapchain.");
 		swapChainExtent_ = {};  // makes it so querying width/height returns 0.
+		swapchainImageExtent_ = {};
 		// We pretend to have a swapchain initialized - though we won't actually render to it.
 		swapchainInited_ = true;
 		return true;
@@ -1413,6 +1414,12 @@ bool VulkanContext::InitSwapchain(VkPres
 	swapChainExtent_.width = clamp(currentExtent.width, surfCapabilities_.minImageExtent.width, surfCapabilities_.maxImageExtent.width);
 	swapChainExtent_.height = clamp(currentExtent.height, surfCapabilities_.minImageExtent.height, surfCapabilities_.maxImageExtent.height);
 
+	// By default the actual swapchain image extent matches the backbuffer extent.
+	// The existing driver-rotation block below may swap both together; the
+	// PPSSPP_DISPLAY_ROTATION override (added further down) only swaps the
+	// backbuffer extent and leaves swapchainImageExtent_ at the physical size.
+	swapchainImageExtent_ = swapChainExtent_;
+
 	INFO_LOG(Log::G3D, "surfCapabilities_.current: %dx%d min: %dx%d max: %dx%d computed: %dx%d",
 		currentExtent.width, currentExtent.height,
 		surfCapabilities_.minImageExtent.width, surfCapabilities_.minImageExtent.height,
@@ -1479,6 +1486,7 @@ bool VulkanContext::InitSwapchain(VkPres
 			g_display.rotation = DisplayRotation::ROTATE_90;
 			g_display.rot_matrix.setRotationZ90();
 			std::swap(swapChainExtent_.width, swapChainExtent_.height);
+			std::swap(swapchainImageExtent_.width, swapchainImageExtent_.height);
 			break;
 		case VK_SURFACE_TRANSFORM_ROTATE_180_BIT_KHR:
 			g_display.rotation = DisplayRotation::ROTATE_180;
@@ -1488,6 +1496,7 @@ bool VulkanContext::InitSwapchain(VkPres
 			g_display.rotation = DisplayRotation::ROTATE_270;
 			g_display.rot_matrix.setRotationZ270();
 			std::swap(swapChainExtent_.width, swapChainExtent_.height);
+			std::swap(swapchainImageExtent_.width, swapchainImageExtent_.height);
 			break;
 		default:
 			_dbg_assert_(false);
@@ -1497,6 +1506,53 @@ bool VulkanContext::InitSwapchain(VkPres
 		preTransform = VK_SURFACE_TRANSFORM_IDENTITY_BIT_KHR;
 	}
 
+	// === muOS rk3576 (and similar): force application-side rotation ===
+	// On some Mali Vulkan drivers using VK_KHR_display, the driver advertises
+	// only IDENTITY in supportedTransforms / currentTransform even on physically
+	// rotated panels. Setting PPSSPP_DISPLAY_ROTATION=90/180/270 forces the
+	// renderer to pre-rotate UI and game content so it appears correctly.
+	//
+	// Critically, swapchainImageExtent_ is left UN-swapped here: those are the
+	// dimensions of the actual VkImage objects used for the swapchain, and the
+	// surface refuses any extent other than the natural panel size.  Only
+	// swapChainExtent_ (the dimensions exposed to the UI via GetBackbufferWidth/
+	// Height) gets swapped, so PPSSPP lays out for landscape while drawing into
+	// portrait swapchain images. Internal Vulkan resource sizing in
+	// VulkanQueueRunner uses GetSwapchainImageWidth/Height to stay consistent
+	// with the real images.
+	{
+		const char *forceRotation = getenv("PPSSPP_DISPLAY_ROTATION");
+		if (forceRotation && *forceRotation) {
+			int rot = atoi(forceRotation);
+			g_display.rot_matrix.setIdentity();
+			switch (rot) {
+			case 90:
+				g_display.rotation = DisplayRotation::ROTATE_90;
+				g_display.rot_matrix.setRotationZ90();
+				std::swap(swapChainExtent_.width, swapChainExtent_.height);
+				break;
+			case 180:
+				g_display.rotation = DisplayRotation::ROTATE_180;
+				g_display.rot_matrix.setRotationZ180();
+				break;
+			case 270:
+				g_display.rotation = DisplayRotation::ROTATE_270;
+				g_display.rot_matrix.setRotationZ270();
+				std::swap(swapChainExtent_.width, swapChainExtent_.height);
+				break;
+			case 0:
+				g_display.rotation = DisplayRotation::ROTATE_0;
+				break;
+			default:
+				WARN_LOG(Log::G3D, "PPSSPP_DISPLAY_ROTATION=%s ignored (use 0/90/180/270)", forceRotation);
+				break;
+			}
+			INFO_LOG(Log::G3D, "PPSSPP_DISPLAY_ROTATION=%d: backbuffer=%dx%d swapchainImage=%dx%d",
+				rot, swapChainExtent_.width, swapChainExtent_.height,
+				swapchainImageExtent_.width, swapchainImageExtent_.height);
+		}
+	}
+
 	// Only log transforms if relevant.
 	if (surfCapabilities_.supportedTransforms != VK_SURFACE_TRANSFORM_IDENTITY_BIT_KHR) {
 		std::string preTransformStr = surface_transforms_to_string(preTransform);
@@ -1512,6 +1568,7 @@ bool VulkanContext::InitSwapchain(VkPres
 			// To keep the size consistent even with pretransform, do this after the swap. Should be fine.
 			// This is fixed in newer PowerVR drivers but I don't know the cutoff.
 			swapChainExtent_.width &= ~31;
+			swapchainImageExtent_.width &= ~31;
 
 			// TODO: Also modify display_xres/display_yres appropriately for scissors to match.
 			// This will get a bit messy. Ideally we should remove that logic from app-android.cpp
@@ -1528,8 +1585,10 @@ bool VulkanContext::InitSwapchain(VkPres
 	swap_chain_info.minImageCount = desiredNumberOfSwapChainImages;
 	swap_chain_info.imageFormat = swapchainFormat_;
 	swap_chain_info.imageColorSpace = VK_COLOR_SPACE_SRGB_NONLINEAR_KHR;
-	swap_chain_info.imageExtent.width = swapChainExtent_.width;
-	swap_chain_info.imageExtent.height = swapChainExtent_.height;
+	// Use the physical extent for actual VkImage creation. In the normal/Android
+	// path this equals swapChainExtent_; under PPSSPP_DISPLAY_ROTATION it differs.
+	swap_chain_info.imageExtent.width = swapchainImageExtent_.width;
+	swap_chain_info.imageExtent.height = swapchainImageExtent_.height;
 	swap_chain_info.preTransform = preTransform;
 	swap_chain_info.imageArrayLayers = 1;
 	swap_chain_info.presentMode = swapchainPresentMode;
diff -urpN a/Common/GPU/Vulkan/VulkanContext.h b/Common/GPU/Vulkan/VulkanContext.h
--- a/Common/GPU/Vulkan/VulkanContext.h	2026-05-09 23:34:27.449146341 +0000
+++ b/Common/GPU/Vulkan/VulkanContext.h	2026-05-09 23:34:47.318261846 +0000
@@ -380,6 +380,18 @@ public:
 	int GetBackbufferWidth() { return (int)swapChainExtent_.width; }
 	int GetBackbufferHeight() { return (int)swapChainExtent_.height; }
 
+	// Physical swapchain image dimensions.  Equal to GetBackbufferWidth/Height
+	// in the normal case (driver-side rotation, or no rotation at all).  When
+	// PPSSPP_DISPLAY_ROTATION is used to force application-side rotation while
+	// the surface forbids extent changes (e.g. Mali VK_KHR_display on rk3576),
+	// the backbuffer dimensions exposed to the UI are the LOGICAL/post-rotation
+	// dimensions, while these getters return the PHYSICAL dimensions of the
+	// actual VkImage objects.  Internal Vulkan resource sizing (depth buffer,
+	// backbuffer render-pass area, RotateRectToDisplay destination) must use
+	// these to stay consistent with the real swapchain images.
+	int GetSwapchainImageWidth() { return (int)swapchainImageExtent_.width; }
+	int GetSwapchainImageHeight() { return (int)swapchainImageExtent_.height; }
+
 	void SetProfilerEnabledPtr(bool *enabled) {
 		for (auto &frame : frame_) {
 			frame.profiler.SetEnabledPtr(enabled);
@@ -500,6 +512,10 @@ private:
 
 	// Swap chain extent
 	VkExtent2D swapChainExtent_{};
+	// Actual VkImage extent for the swapchain images.  Differs from swapChainExtent_
+	// only when application-side rotation is forced (PPSSPP_DISPLAY_ROTATION) on a
+	// surface that won't accept rotated extents.
+	VkExtent2D swapchainImageExtent_{};
 
 	VulkanContext::CreateInfo createInfo_{};
 
